  <prompt>
    Rewrite docs/guides/RECORD-HEADER-PCF-AUTHORING-GUIDE.md (~354 lines) from "how to write a new per-entity
    PCF" to "how to configure the header for a new entity" — the per-entity recipe becomes actively wrong the day
    R2 ships. Roughly 170-190 lines (≈50-55%) are replaced or heavily revised; ~120 survive. Author the new content
    FROM SHIPPED CODE, not by diffing the old guide — the old guide has ALREADY drifted from v1.0.20 and cannot be
    trusted as a baseline.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE platform developer and technical writer. Expert in PCF manifests, the R2 RecordHeader configuration
    model, and the docs-guide conventions. Follow ADRs strictly.
  </role>

  <goal>
    docs/guides/RECORD-HEADER-PCF-AUTHORING-GUIDE.md teaches the R2 workflow (bind Spaarke.Records.RecordHeader on
    a main form, author layoutJson, rely on derived defaults) with zero surviving references to the retired
    per-entity recipe, the bundle-optimization triad section preserved verbatim, and every code claim verified
    against the shipped RecordHeader control.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      FR-27 (spec.md) and design.md §3.1 scoping note. The old guide's core recipe (clone a thin per-entity PCF)
      was withdrawn 2026-08-21. KNOWN DRIFT in the old guide — this is WHY authoring must start from shipped code,
      and each of these must NOT survive into the rewrite:
      (a) its manifest example shows a recordId input-only control, but actual v1.0.20 shipped boundField (bound) +
      title + showVersion — and R2 adds layoutJson;
      (b) its modal sizes are stale: SmartTodo "85%×85%" is now the openTodos filtered launch, Notepad "70%×80%"
      is now 25%×35%;
      (c) it documents a recordSummary hook parameter retired at v1.0.10;
      (d) it repeats the ADR-011 "typed components — no runtime schemas" line that design.md §12 debunks (ADR-011
      contains no such rule);
      (e) it claims platform-library theming removes the need for a manual FluentProvider — R1 live QA proved the
      manual wrap IS required (Fluent portals mount outside the PCF subtree);
      (f) line 86 says the version number appears in "four" locations — the correct count is FIVE (ADR-020).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">docs/guides/RECORD-HEADER-PCF-AUTHORING-GUIDE.md</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/pcf/RecordHeader/control/ControlManifest.Input.xml</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/pcf/RecordHeader/control/index.ts</file>
