      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/hooks/toolbarLaunchDefaults.ts</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="080" status="pending">Matter parity QA complete — the RecordHeader control is shipped, bound on all six entities, and stable; the guide documents final reality, not a moving target.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-27">Author every new section FROM the shipped code (RecordHeader manifest, view, resolver, toolbarLaunchDefaults) — never by paraphrasing or diffing the old guide's per-entity sections. Each manifest/property/size claim in the new guide must be traceable to a shipped file.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-27">PRESERVE the "Bundle Optimization — MANDATORY for Consuming PCFs" section (currently lines ~206-265, the ~57-line triad block: featureconfig.json + webpack.config.js + deep-path imports) VERBATIM — it is still correct and still mandatory (NFR-08). Heading anchors referenced elsewhere must keep working.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-020">Correct the version-locations count from "four" to FIVE everywhere it appears (currently line 86), consistent with PCF-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The rewrite scope is docs/guides/RECORD-HEADER-PCF-AUTHORING-GUIDE.md ONLY. Do not edit PCF-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md, the pattern pointer (that is task 086), or any code file.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Surviving content (~120 lines: shared-primitives overview, Notepad launch contract, testing/deploy skeleton, troubleshooting, FAQ, references) is kept only where re-verified against shipped code — stale modal sizes and the retired recordSummary param in those sections must be corrected, not preserved.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
