  <notes>
    COMPLETED 2026-08-27, PULLED FORWARD ahead of its `080` dependency at owner request ("this needs
    to be fixed/updated"). The dependency was about finality rather than content: the control is
    shipped and UAT-passed at v1.1.11, and the maker recipe does not change when Matter migrates.
    Leaving it until after 080 meant leaving a live hazard in place -- the guide was teaching the
    RETIRED per-entity-PCF recipe end-to-end, which is exactly the wrong instruction for any agent or
    maker who found it.

    Rewritten from shipped code, 353 -> ~250 lines. It now OPENS with an explicit stop-sign for the
    retired approach rather than burying the correction. Reframed from "author a new PCF" to
    "configure the one control": binding recipe, layoutJson schema reference, manifest properties,
    sparkle behaviour, and the two 🚨 traps (MOVE-don't-delete the raw fields; edit ALL THREE form
    factors). Developer material retained where still true -- the bundle-optimization triad (still
    mandatory), the two FAILED bundle "fixes" that must not be re-derived, the Notepad/SmartTodo
    launch contracts, and the G-12/G-13/G-14 rules. Troubleshooting now leads with the two console
    diagnostics the control emits.

    Also fixed FOUR broken ADR links, three of which were inherited from the original: ADR-024 and
    ADR-028 live in `.claude/adr/`, not `docs/adr/`, and ADR-006's filename is
    `ADR-006-prefer-pcf-over-webresources.md`. All relative links verified to resolve.

    Follow-up: re-check after task 080 in case the Matter migration surfaces anything new.
  </notes>

